cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PowderBench, its data or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "PowderBench: a live, contamination-free benchmark for mountain snowfall forecasting"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nakas
    given-names: Andrew
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrewnakas/powderbench"
url: "https://powderbench.com"
license: MIT
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
keywords:
  - snowfall
  - weather forecasting
  - benchmark
  - SNOTEL
  - machine learning
abstract: >-
  PowderBench scores 24-72 hour mountain snowfall forecasts from humans, ML
  models and AI agents against quality-controlled observations at ~2,400
  stations across North America, the Alps and the southern hemisphere, next
  to the world's operational weather models. Rounds ask about weather that
  has not happened yet, so the benchmark cannot be memorized.
